; shown.claims — a property that singles out a situation, and the queries it
; asks to be answered there. On query_rows.writ the watchdog is captured at the
; initial situation, so `no-capture` fails with an EMPTY route — the violating
; situation is #0 — and `captured` is answered at exactly that situation.
(property no-capture "no bureau is ever captured"
  (never (some (b bureau) (is b.independence captured)))
  (show captured))

(query captured
  (where (b bureau))
  (is b.independence captured))
